ed  towards the top of the pyramid the long  tail of small podcasts with small  audiences barely make any income at all  that's put a real premium on  discoverability or how easy it is to  find your show and it's also made apple  and spotify into gatekeepers there's a  bit of a conflict of interest there of  course because apple and spotify both  produce their own content too they have  both the opportunity and the incentive  to give their own shows preferential  treatment here's matt deegan the  creative director of folder media which  produces some podcasts  will  the curatorial places on spotify become  more about spotify originals than they  do about the party content now i don't  think i'll ever go 100 but you know  already probably 20 of curatorial is is  is to spotify and  spotify don't produce nearly anything  like 20 of the big podcasts out there  there's also little stopping them from  following the playbook pioneered by  social media companies about a decade  ago brands and public figures alike were  encouraged to build public profiles with  the promise they'll be able to reach  huge audiences but over time the  algorithm was tweaked meaning that you  might have a million followers but you'd  only perhaps reach one percent of them  if you didn't pay for more prominent  placement  that's also now the risk for podcasters  that it starts to become paid to play  spotify is already doing this in the  music space artists can pay to promote  their new releases  in turn that's why audio giants like the  bbc and luminary are building their own  apps they don't want to be beholden to  the whims of the gatekeepers there's a  real contest for your ears and they're  turning up the volume  [Music]  you
 

